From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:23:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] cheetah: keep app odex on /system, not system_other

BoardConfigMainlineCommon.mk turns on BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX, which
moves the odex/vdex of every preopted app (SystemUIGoogle, SettingsGoogle,
LineageParts, ...) into system_other.img (179 MB here). Google's factory
images flash that image to the inactive slot and cppreopts copies it in on
first boot; an OTA never writes it, so those apps start every update with
no AOT code and SystemUI gestures hitch until background dexopt runs.
Build them into /system instead. Same as husky's shusky 0003.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cheetah/BoardConfig.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
index d7b898b..627e904 100644
--- a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -22,3 +22,10 @@ SYSTEM_EXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLICY_DIRS += \
 include $(DEVICE_PATH)/BoardConfigCommon.mk
 
 include $(VENDOR_PATH)/BoardConfigVendor.mk
+
+# Keep app odex on /system rather than system_other. Only a factory flash
+# writes system_other to the inactive slot; zip and OTA installs never do, so
+# SystemUIGoogle, SettingsGoogle and the other preopted priv-apps lose their
+# AOT code after every update and run interpreted/JIT until background
+# dexopt catches up (~180 MB, well inside super).
+BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX :=
-- 
